scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: null
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified observation 17 notes NotFound falls back to defaults
    correctly, but never flags that ALL other error types (parse errors, permission
    denied) are also swallowed. The from_file_or_default pattern is noted as verified,
    not flagged.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified observation 14: 'ServerError display suppresses the\
    \ raw body: write!(f, \"server error (HTTP {status})\") \u2014 the second field\
    \ is ignored in Display.' However, the broader CliError Display with Io(#[error(transparent)])\
    \ leaking OS details to stderr was not flagged. Partial catch \u2014 ServerError\
    \ sanitized but Io variant still leaks."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests (siem_client_test.rs:103-130) checking\
    \ CRLF in tenant_id. Reviewer observation 11 also flags 'tenant field is Option<String>\
    \ not TenantId'. However, the underlying type remains raw String \u2014 CRLF is\
    \ stripped but TenantId newtype not used."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added dependencies with direct version strings (clap_complete, comfy-table,
    csv, dirs, reqwest, toml) to workspace Cargo.toml. Neither TEA, Dev, nor Reviewer
    flagged that crate Cargo.toml should use workspace = true references instead of
    direct versions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer observation 4: ''RawConfig has no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].
    A typo like api_ulr = "..." will be silently ignored, and the user will get the
    default value with no warning. This is a usability trap.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)) in the test suite. TEA wrote the tests but included this logical flaw.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config with no assert).
    TEA wrote the test but did not include meaningful assertions.
